==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ang|hyċġġan|hyċġean|hiċġan}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*hugjaną|t=think, consider}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|huggian}}, {{cog|goh|huggen}}, {{cog|non|hyggja}}, {{cog|got|𐌷𐌿𐌲𐌾𐌰𐌽}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ang|/ˈhyd.d͡ʒɑn/}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|hyċġan}}

# to [[think]]
# to think about, to [[consider]]

====Usage notes====
The conjugation table below shows the inherited forms of ''hyċġan'', with ''hy(ċ)ġ-'' throughout the present tense and ''hogd-'' throughout the past. These are the normal forms in Early West Saxon. In the other dialects and Late West Saxon, the past is often inflected like a class II weak verb, with ''hogod-'' ~ ''hogad-'', and the present forms are often based on ''hogian''.

